        "TextSection": {
            "TextSectionType": "Definition",
            "Contents": "T-B+ severe combined immunodeficiency (SCID) is a group of rare monogenic primary immunodeficiency disorders characterized by a lack of functional peripheral T lymphocytes with presence of B lymphocytes resulting in early-onset severe respiratory viral bacterial or fungal infections diarrhea and failure to thrive."
